PREDICTIONS -- the Opus seat's F2 legs against repair 16's frozen probe (table16_20260926/crime_width_probe.table16.py,
md5 5f770991, 226 rows).  Written BEFORE batch f2a starts (this file's mtime is the order proof).

  S_rst4clr     sw08 halts, ctlrst sw halt                      224/226  CONTROL=FAIL (sw08 halts is a CONTROL row)
                -- the accepted 4-byte 0x800 at latch CLEAR no longer halts: sw08's and ctlrst sw's RAM trips run.
                   `rst 4w' (latch SET) stays green; `ctlrst sw msg' stays 1 (the clear still runs).
  M_ctldebug    none                                            226/226  CONTROL=OK   -- an ESCAPE: every session that
                   counts `CRIME_CONTROL: unimplemented' is stepped, and debug() prints while stepping.
  H_rstclr4clr  ctlrst sw msg                                   225/226  CONTROL=OK
                -- the HARD_RESET clear skipped only for a 4-byte write with the latch CLEAR: only ctlrst sw's 0x800 is in
                   that cell (`sw08 halts' holds one too, but no row counts text there; `rst 4w msg' runs latch SET).
  E_endlatch    rearm ctl msg                                   225/226  CONTROL=OK
                -- the ENDIANESS clear skipped only with the latch SET: the rearm session's two 0x0100 writes print (6);
                   `latch ctl msg' (latch CLEAR) stays 4.

Discriminator (disc_f2.py, one short session each, base vs M_ctldebug): a free-running accepted `sw 0x0001' at +0x08
prints the CONTROL text once on base and NOT AT ALL under M_ctldebug; the same store stepped prints once on both.
